      "side": 1,
      "message": "IWBN to have an example for the reverse direction too, i.e. `extern \"C++\"`. In my vello FFI crate I have both generated and hand-coded C++ headers. The hand-coded C++ header defines an interface to be implemented by the client and the rust code calls out to it:\n\n   * The C++ header: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/665656/3/third_party/vello/include/vello_cpp/path_iterator.h\n   * The FFI bridge: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/665656/3/third_party/vello/src/lib.rs#126\n\nCurrently I keep this header in an `include/` directory that I explicitly set up in the GN rule https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/665656/4/third_party/vello/BUILD.gn#27 so it\u0027s visible to the client and my custom `build.rs` (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/665656/4/third_party/vello/build.rs#9) configures cxxbuild to look for it when compiling Rust.\n\nHow should I structure this in the Bazel world?",
